{
  "_comment": "Cases for the /mcp workbench tools (pflow_sde, pflow_what_if, pflow_optimize) and the composition tools (pflow_bundle_*). A workbench case is one tool call on a fixture (path relative to parity/). A composition case is one tool call on a composition: `composition` names an entry of `compositions` (the {instances, links} that bundle.open takes: the catalog composition native builds), or `bundle_file` is a PetriNetBundle document (path relative to parity/); pflow_bundle_example takes its composition as its own args. parity/native/gen/src/bundle.rs says what native answers. parity/native/gen turns it into the pflow-native commands the editor runs for it and writes their answer to mcp_goldens.json; cmd/webserver/mcp_workbench_parity_test.go replays the call through the Go tool and compares. `tolerance` (relative) applies to fractional numbers only, and `why` says why it is needed; a case without it is compared exactly, and an optimize case's linearly sampled rates are compared exactly either way. See parity/native/README.md.",
